:["attack"]},"_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":null}},"type":"action","effects":[],"_key":"!actors.items!SmSg3DIbzqGq7SZ1.0VnHFn3wn3nNZ2Tp"},{"_id":"pdtNmk8Zc7lN4BFF","_stats":{"coreVersion":"14.361","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"8.5.0","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.Tkd8sH4pwFIPzqTr"},"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/OneAction.webp","name":"Grab","sort":800000,"system":{"actionType":{"value":"action"},"actions":{"value":1},"category":"offensive","description":{"value":"<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Grab]</p>"},"publication":{"license":"OGL","remaster":false,"title":"Pathfinder Bestiary"},"rules":[],"slug":"grab","traits":{"rarity":"common","value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":null}},"type":"action","effects":[],"_key":"!actors.items!SmSg3DIbzqGq7SZ1.pdtNmk8Zc7lN4BFF"}],"name":"Gashadokuro","system":{"abilities":{"cha":{"mod":3},"con":{"mod":5},"dex":{"mod":4},"int":{"mod":-3},"str":{"mod":8},"wis":{"mod":3}},"attributes":{"ac":{"details":"","value":33},"allSaves":{"value":""},"hp":{"details":"void healing","max":230,"temp":0,"value":230},"immunities":[{"type":"bleed"},{"type":"death-effects"},{"type":"disease"},{"type":"paralyzed"},{"type":"poison"},{"type":"unconscious"}],"resistances":[{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"electricity","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10},{"type":"piercing","value":10},{"type":"slashing","value":10}],"speed":{"otherSpeeds":[],"special":"","value":25}},"details":{"blurb":"","languages":{"details":"(can't speak any language)","value":["common"]},"level":{"value":13},"privateNotes":"","publicNotes":"<p>The dreaded gashadokuro is an undead haunter of the night, spawning as a giant skeleton that rises from the earth in the aftermath of a mass starvation event. These enormous creatures then seek to inflict their unending hunger on the living.</p>\n<p>A gashadokuro that comes about due to a poor growing season is more prone to stalk remote village farmlands at night, while a gashadokuro that arose from the victims of a government-instigated food shortage has few compunctions about stomping straight into bustling cities in broad daylight. These latter gashadokuro even seem to target aristocrats and government authorities-whether or not they were the same politicians whose negligence resulted in the famine in the first place-leading many to believe that the gashadokuro seeks to slake its thirst for revenge even more than it seeks to sate its unending hunger.</p>","publication":{"license":"OGL","remaster":false,"title":"Pathfinder Book of the Dead"}},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"perception":{"details":"","mod":24,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"}]},"resources":{},"saves":{"fortitude":{"saveDetail":"","value":26},"reflex":{"saveDetail":"","value":21},"will":{"saveDetail":"","value":24}},"skills":{"athletics":{"base":27},"intimidation":{"base":24}},"traits":{"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"huge"},"value":["evil","undead","unholy"]},"_migration":{"version":0.959,"previous":null}},"type":"npc","_stats":{"coreVersion":"14.361","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"8.5.0","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.book-of-the-dead-bestiary.Actor.XrSjNpkJkBO6ysRG"},"effects":[],"_key":"!actors!SmSg3DIbzqGq7SZ1","folder":null,"prototypeToken":{"texture":{"src":"modules/pf2e-dungeon-crawl/assets/creature-art/book-of-the-dead-bestiary/gashadokuro-lob.webp"}},"flags":{"pf2e-dungeon-crawl":{"artEntryId":"book_of_the_dead_bestiary__gashadokuro","sourcePack":"pf2e.book-of-the-dead-bestiary","sourceDocId":"XrSjNpkJkBO6ysRG"}}}